  "notes": [
    "CT-PLM-2: this template needs 4 or more weeks of logged RPE or RIR ratings; otherwise the lifter stays on 5/3/1 and this is offered as the alternative.",
    "CT-PLM-3: week 1's range is centred on the load the chart gives for that week's reps at its RPE target from the current e1RM; weeks 2 to 4 raise the midpoint by the weekly step (the chart's rise, capped per lift). Logged top sets move later weeks only through an IL-20 re-issue.",
    "CT-PLM-5, CT-PLM-20: the top-set RPE rises about 0.25 a week (7.5, 7.5-8, 8, 8-8.5 in PREP 2) and is written as RIR (2-3, 2-3, 2, 1-2).",
    "CT-PLM-13: accessory RIR steps down from week 1's base (weeks 2 and 3 at 0.5 below, week 4 at 1 below, deload at 1 above and at least 3). Free-weight compounds start at RIR 2 so they never reach 0 (A-7).",
    "CT-PLM-6: an 8 to 12-week prep is PREP 2 then PEAK; a shortened PREP 2 is flagged to the lifter. PEAK is generated as its own block (phase 'peak') from the e1RMs PREP 2 produced.",
    "CT-PLM-11: PEAK keeps accessories in its first 2 weeks only; the competition lifts and the close-grip bench carry on.",
    "Main-lift warm-ups are not computed: L-6 is a 5/3/1 rule. The movement prep in the hand-over covers it (P-19).",
    "CT-PLM-15 to CT-PLM-19 (attempt band, taper timing, weigh-in, class and any cut) are not part of this program (attempts: the ironledger-meet-attempts skill; any weight cut: a coach or sports dietitian)."
  ]
